1
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:20,846
Hello. Hello there.

2
00:00:20,846 --> 00:01:07,229
Are you ready for lunch with your grandpa?

3
00:01:07,229 --> 00:01:11,471
Oh! Hi, Grandpa. Yes, of course, I am, but my mind isn't.

4
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:13,631
What's the matter, Susan?

5
00:01:13,631 --> 00:01:15,489
A real dilemma.

6
00:01:15,489 --> 00:01:17,427
Does it have anything to do with you and Harry?

7
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:21,389
Yes, but I don't know where to start.

8
00:01:21,389 --> 00:01:26,921
Maybe I can help. Tell me what it is, Susan.

9
00:01:26,921 --> 00:01:32,317
Thanks, Grandpa. Please sit down.

10
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:38,273
Oh! Harry has been offered a job in Los Angeles.

11
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:42,251
Well, this is something to think about.

12
00:01:42,251 --> 00:01:45,829
There are so many things to consider. There's Michelle.

13
00:01:45,829 --> 00:01:50,777
I wonder if a move would be a bad thing for her. And my job.

14
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:53,656
I don't know if I can get a good job in Los Angeles.

15
00:01:53,656 --> 00:01:59,118
And what about our family?

16
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:01,398
Can I tell you what I think?

17
00:02:01,398 --> 00:02:02,096
Tell me.

18
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:05,449
I think that you're very successful

19
00:02:05,449 --> 00:02:11,030
and that you have a fantastic reputation in the toy industry.

20
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:14,008
I think you could talk to Mr. Marchetta,

21
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:15,259
and I think

22
00:02:15,259 --> 00:02:19,964
he could help you find a real good job in Los Angeles.

23
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:22,942
He was very helpful to me, remember?

24
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,920
I suppose I could call him.

25
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:28,898
But I'm not so sure that I want to leave New York,

26
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:30,898
you, and the rest of our family.

27
00:02:30,898 --> 00:02:32,101
Well, I'm not going to kid you, Susan.

28
00:02:32,101 --> 00:02:33,451
You know we'd all miss you.

29
00:02:33,451 --> 00:02:37,354
But this should be your decision.

30
00:02:37,354 --> 00:02:41,370
It's something that only you and Harry can work out.

31
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:46,766
If moving to L.A. is in Harry's best interest,

32
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:51,224
I have to do what I can do to support him.

33
00:02:51,224 --> 00:02:52,722
In every marriage,

34
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:57,700
sacrifices have to be made by one partner from time to time.

35
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:01,656
And what about Michelle?

36
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:03,856
Well, what do you think?

37
00:03:03,856 --> 00:03:07,612
I think Michelle is better off staying where she is.

38
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:09,300
What does she think?

39
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,160
I don't know for sure.

40
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,922
Well, you'll have to ask her.

41
00:03:12,922 --> 00:03:15,470
I think I'm going to have a talk with Mr. Marchetta

42
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:17,145
and get his feelings about my leaving.

43
00:03:17,145 --> 00:03:20,603
And about helping me find a job in Los Angeles.

44
00:03:20,603 --> 00:03:21,683
Good idea.

45
00:03:21,683 --> 00:03:24,834
I'll call him right now. No point in delaying.

46
00:03:24,834 --> 00:03:25,479
Thanks, Grandpa.

47
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:40,055
Harry, it's the perfect job for you. You'll love it. Harry

48
00:03:40,055 --> 00:03:43,347
It's a big decision for me, Bill.

49
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:46,325
And I have to discuss it with my wife.

50
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:47,765
I don't know if it's right for her.

51
00:03:47,765 --> 00:03:51,743
She'll love it. It's a once-in-a-lifetime offer, Harry.

52
00:03:51,743 --> 00:03:53,608
OK. Tell it to me again.

53
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:55,259
The company is Craft and Craft,

54
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:58,237
the biggest accounting company in the country.

55
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:00,228
I know the company well. It's big.

56
00:04:00,228 --> 00:04:01,215
The biggest.

57
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:17,257
Yeah, yeah. The biggest. When do I have to let you know?

58
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:24,727
Talk it over. Think it over. Let me know by the end of the week.

59
00:04:24,727 --> 00:04:26,785
When would we have to move?

60
00:04:26,785 --> 00:04:27,620
As soon as possible.

61
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:42,906
I also have my daughter to consider.

62
00:04:42,906 --> 00:04:52,590
I don't want to interrupt her school year.

63
00:04:52,590 --> 00:04:56,458
Let me know by the end of the week.

64
00:04:56,458 --> 00:04:59,411
It's a great opportunity for you, Harry.

65
00:04:59,411 --> 00:05:00,104
Believe me.

66
00:05:00,104 --> 00:05:03,752
I know.

67
00:05:03,752 --> 00:05:11,348
Craft and Craft is the biggest in the country. Craft and Crraft

68
00:05:11,348 --> 00:05:15,664
Yeah, I know. The biggest.

69
00:05:15,664 --> 00:05:21,620
I think Michelle is asleep now. Let's talk.

70
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:23,334
I met with Bill York today.

71
00:05:23,334 --> 00:05:32,794
And I talked with Mr. Marchetta. Did York make the offer?

72
00:05:32,794 --> 00:05:38,287
Yup. He asked me if I want the job.

73
00:05:38,287 --> 00:05:40,737
That's exciting, Harry. What was it?

74
00:05:40,737 --> 00:05:41,487
A vice-presidency

75
00:05:41,487 --> 00:05:44,965
with the biggest accounting company in the country--

76
00:05:44,965 --> 00:05:47,336
Craft and Craft. Craft and Crraft。

77
00:05:47,336 --> 00:05:51,399
Aren't you excited about that?

78
00:05:51,399 --> 00:05:54,606
Sure I am. But there's so much more to consider.

79
00:05:54,606 --> 00:05:55,748
I talked to Mr. Marchetta.

80
00:05:55,748 --> 00:06:00,893
What did he say? Did you tell him about me?

81
00:06:00,893 --> 00:06:21,179
Of course, Harry. I want what's best for you,

82
00:06:21,179 --> 00:06:24,586
and I think I can get a good job

83
00:06:24,586 --> 00:06:25,871
through Mr. Marchetta

84
00:06:25,871 --> 00:06:30,113
in Los Angeles also.

85
00:06:30,113 --> 00:06:30,780
You're kidding.

86
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:52,038
No, I'm not kidding.

87
00:06:52,038 --> 00:06:55,456
I talked with him, and he understands completely.

88
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:57,414
He has a major toy buyer in Los Angeles,

89
00:06:57,414 --> 00:07:11,804
and he's pretty sure that I can get a good job there.

90
00:07:11,804 --> 00:07:12,204
Unbelievable!

91
00:07:12,204 --> 00:07:24,416
But I think we should talk to Michelle about all of this.

92
00:07:24,416 --> 00:07:44,562
You're right. We'll talk to her about it.

93
00:07:44,562 --> 00:07:49,654
And how do you feel about taking the job in Los Angeles?

94
00:07:49,654 --> 00:08:02,949
How should I feel?

95
00:08:02,949 --> 00:08:05,407
It's the biggest company in the country.

96
00:08:05,407 --> 00:08:09,135
Well, then you feel good about taking it?

97
00:08:09,135 --> 00:08:12,135
Well ... I feel fine about it. Why shouldn't I?
